    <title>Sparse
  Attention</title>
    <summary>  We study sparse attention for long-context language models and show that a learned routing of
  tokens to a small set of memory slots keeps accuracy within one point of dense attention while cutting
  memory use by a factor of eight on documents of up to one million tokens.
</summary>
